<description>
Complete the broken blue grid lines by painting red into their missing background cells.

Input structure:
- A black background contains one blue interrupted rectilinear grid.
- The foreground bbox contains the whole grid.
- A horizontal line is marked by at least one horizontally adjacent pair of blue
  pixels in its row; a vertical line is marked by at least one vertically
  adjacent pair of blue pixels in its column.

Rule:
- Keep all input pixels unchanged.
- Across the foreground bbox, fill background cells red on every marked
  horizontal row and every marked vertical column.

Key insight:
- Isolated blue pixels can be intersections of the opposite orientation, while
  adjacent blue pairs reveal which rows and columns are actual grid lines.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "blue interrupted rectilinear grid on black background; marked rows contain a horizontal blue adjacency and marked columns contain a vertical blue adjacency",
  "transform": "within the foreground bbox, paint red on background cells along every marked row and marked column; preserve existing blue pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 9-13 rows x 13 cols, black (0) background
  structure: |
    An interrupted rectilinear grid of blue (1) pixels on black.
    "Marked rows" have >=1 horizontally-adjacent blue pair within the bbox.
    "Marked cols" have >=1 vertically-adjacent blue pair within the bbox.
  bbox: 7-9 rows x 7-9 cols, defines the foreground extent
  marked_rows: 2-3; always include first and last row of bbox
  marked_cols: 2-3; always include first and last col of bbox
  spacing: 2-8 between consecutive marked rows; 2-8 between consecutive marked cols
  blue_placement:
    on_marked_lines: each marked row/col has 22-44% gap (black) cells; rest blue
    off_marked_lines: blue appears ONLY at intersections of (non-marked row, marked col); never on (non-marked row, non-marked col)
    each_marked_line: must contain >=1 adjacent blue pair (run of >=2) for detection
  padding: 1-4 black rows/cols on each side between grid edge and bbox
  transform:
    within bbox, fill black cells red (2) on every marked row and marked col
    all existing blue pixels preserved unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size (9-13 x 13) and bbox position with 1-4 padding per side
    2. Choose 2-3 marked rows and 2-3 marked cols within bbox; first/last row and col of bbox must be marked; spacings >=2
    3. Build complete output grid lines (all blue+red on marked rows/cols within bbox)
    4. On each marked row, randomly convert 22-44% of cells to gap positions; on each marked col likewise; ensure at least one adjacent-blue pair survives per line
    5. On non-marked rows, place blue at each marked-col position with ~50-80% probability (these represent interrupted vertical line segments)
    6. Build input by replacing all red cells with black (undo the fill); blue stays
    7. Validate: every marked row/col has an adjacent blue pair; no non-marked row/col has one
